<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:39:21Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Sweden's centre-left opposition wins election, SVT says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7346bbdaf3c4cd217c0ffd9d2acdb33564af4319be4db08c74f064706a49299</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:39:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T19:21:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sweden-s-centre-left-opposition-wins-election-svt-says--9f32c973e85d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/sweden-s-centre-left-opposition-wins-election-svt-says" /><summary type="html">Sweden's centre-left opposition has defeated the incumbent right-wing governing bloc by the slimmest of margins, public broadcaster ​SVT ‌said on Wednesday, after 99% ⁠of the votes in Sunday's parliamentary election had been counted. FRANCE 24's Paul Rhys reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>The 28th state? Carney's Canada draws closer to European Union</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f988d9d0fd1ed9c43b10679e970c777e359fa90892e0dcb1803b78f9dfce1028</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:37:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T18:19:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260916-the-28th-state-carney-s-canada-draws-closer-to-european-union--94d6c63dedef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260916-the-28th-state-carney-s-canada-draws-closer-to-european-union" /><summary type="html">With a US president who talks of making Canada the 51st state, its leader in Europe where it’s not quite the EU's 28th state on offer, but something the president of the European Commission is calling ‘associate membership’. We’ll ask what that means, how it differs from the close status afforded to the likes of Iceland, Norway, Switzerland and the UK which Carney’s also visiting ahead of his own Strasbourg speech Thursday before the European Parliament.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Ivorian footballer Malick Yalcouyé falsely accused of lying about his age</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:555cbec7ba7efbb43b72c43bf6a09bd42431a6270c3a51dfef39aba81c9f62bb</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:37:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T16:03:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-ivorian-footballer-malick-yalcouy_-falsely-accused-of-lying-about-his-age--2513b388a450.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-ivorian-footballer-malick-yalcouy%C3%A9-falsely-accused-of-lying-about-his-age" /><summary type="html">During a Premier League match between Chelsea and Brighton, social media users started spreading rumours that 20-year-old Ivorian footballer Malick Yalcouyé is older than he claims to be. The rumours gained such proportion that the youth club where he trained decided to post photos of Yalcouyé throughout the years. Recently, similar accusations were made against the new Real Madrid striker Yan Diomandé.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Former Kosovo president sentenced to 25 years for war crimes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b27eff38e4be88ab1b40b6c04cd1562253a17fd2357fa2f32c43c64387869a85</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:39:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T12:55:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-former-kosovo-president-sentenced-to-25-years-for-war-crimes--5d1bf97bde2e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-former-kosovo-president-sentenced-to-25-years-for-war-crimes" /><summary type="html">Former Kosovo President Hashim Thaci was found guilty of war crimes committed as part of the Kosovo Liberation Army including murder, torture and illegal arrests by a tribunal in The Hague on Wednesday. Thaci was sentenced to 25 ​years in prison alongside fellow former KLA figures who were also found guilty and sentenced.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU chief invites Canada to be first-ever ‘associate member’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f25db3673591498085bff1452a8b076036d597cbcb130793aae6f22a11dfb32f</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:39:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T12:22:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-eu-chief-pitches-associate-member-status-for-canada-as-both-seek-to-pivot-away-from-us--d7bebc685bca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-eu-chief-pitches-associate-member-status-for-canada-as-both-seek-to-pivot-away-from-us" /><summary type="html">EU chief Ursula von der Leyen raised the possibility on Wednesday that Canada could become the European Union’s first “associate member” during the annual State of the European Union speech, at which Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney was present. Carney has been pursuing closer ties with the EU as both seek to pivot away from the US.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian drone attack on bus kills five in Ukraine's southeast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3573692a0f1d4f037eacabf9ccdcc6a8be3c35745152cb7d159dc1db1cba9057</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:39:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T07:37:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-russian-drone-attack-on-bus-kills-five-in-ukraine-s-southeast--7488d3d9c757.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-russian-drone-attack-on-bus-kills-five-in-ukraine-s-southeast" /><summary type="html">Five people were killed and at least seven more were injured in a Russian drone attack on a passenger bus near the frontline in Ukraine's southeast on Wednesday, the regional governor said.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU chief calls for creation of ‘European Security Council’, backs partnership with Canada</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85f5572d12b19f600ff8bbe36ef70dea5e59085460c4f39605ad99636a226aa2</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:39:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T05:20:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-live-eu-chief-ursula-von-der-leyen-gives-state-of-the-union-address--62d886b96249.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-live-eu-chief-ursula-von-der-leyen-gives-state-of-the-union-address" /><summary type="html">EU chief Ursula von der Leyen called for the creation of a "European Security Council", with countries including Britain and Ukraine, in her State of the European Union speech to the European Parliament in Strasbourg on Wednesday. Addressing this year's special guest, Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney, von der Leyen said she wants to open the door for Canada to become the bloc's first associate member.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France stalls EU Russia sanctions renewal over oligarch de-listing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d3c535cea8b8e394426df39b9405bbfee66281c49e5f9a40ccee0555105e7a2</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T21:46:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-stalls-eu-russia-sanctions-renewal-over-oligarch-de-listing--887f2b942b54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/france-stalls-eu-russia-sanctions-renewal-over-oligarch-de-listing" /><summary type="html">European Union envoys have pushed back the expiry of EU Russia sanctions listings by ​seven days until September 22, a spokesperson for the EU's Irish presidency said on Monday, after failing to agree on a six-month renewal. At issue is whether to de-list Russian-Uzbek billionaire Alisher Usmanov. France has joined ​Slovakia in ‌a call to remove him, citing national security concerns, EU diplomats ⁠said. FRANCE 24's August Hakansson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>NATO jets down drone over Lithuania as Russian ship fires flares at Danish helicopter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e6e7c0f1da58837fa52af7bc876c833d132f7e3f0219ceae190ab3439615c46</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T20:26:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260915-nato-jets-down-drone-over-lithuania-as-russian-ship-fires-flares-at-danish-helicopter--3a8c3b0b02a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260915-nato-jets-down-drone-over-lithuania-as-russian-ship-fires-flares-at-danish-helicopter" /><summary type="html">NATO fighter jets shot down a drone that entered Lithuanian airspace and Denmark accused a Russian frigate of firing flares at a Danish military helicopter on Tuesday, in incidents that heightened tensions along the alliance’s eastern flank.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Analysts call for step-up in response to Russia after Denmark, Lithuania incidents</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3b43b7d2cdcba8a9fb403b4adaca5dd2c0d7d9b15e63fa81b49ecbc0da9fa65</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T19:23:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/analysts-call-for-step-up-in-response-to-russia-after-denmark-lithuania-incidents--af9e3a44a66f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/analysts-call-for-step-up-in-response-to-russia-after-denmark-lithuania-incidents" /><summary type="html">The European Union accused Russia on Tuesday of the "reckless" firing of flares at a Danish frigate which, with the shooting down of a drone over Lithuania, heightened the continent's anxiety over the Ukraine-Russia war. Danish analysts are calling for NATO and the EU to step up their response to Russia, according to FRANCE 24's Copenhagen correspondent Trine Villemann.</summary></entry><entry><title>Paris ex-mayor says 'collective failure' led to abuse of children in school care</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48c7d857954f14b73abf3ea371202f9446ec4ef8aadf9ca0bc9e3febeff97353</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T15:27:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260915-paris-ex-mayor-says-collective-failure-led-to-abuse-of-children-in-school-care--33d943e8d92c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260915-paris-ex-mayor-says-collective-failure-led-to-abuse-of-children-in-school-care" /><summary type="html">Former Paris mayor Anne Hidalgo acknowledged a “collective failure” to protect children on Tuesday as police investigate more than 200 allegations of violence, mistreatment and sexual abuse at the French capital’s state-run nurseries and primary schools for over more than a decade.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>NATO downs drone over Lithuania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:731801b8f038d8b744ab978f1a8d99d6a326149b6166d173b74a70ba1e5d2ce9</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T02:19:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260915-nato-fighter-jets-shoot-down-drone-over-lithuania-after-latest-incursion--dda4777e115a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260915-nato-fighter-jets-shoot-down-drone-over-lithuania-after-latest-incursion" /><summary type="html">NATO scrambled fighter jets overnight to ​shoot down a drone over Lithuania after the latest incursion on the alliance's eastern flank. In a separate incident, Denmark said a Russian warship fired two emergency flares at a Danish helicopter in the Baltic Sea, adding that the Russian ambassador had been summoned over the "reckless action". Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky says Ukraine ready to de-escalate if Russia halts strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5764b1d5fd94d6e360f5e36cf34e2e94598f214df063171c4ba5e5be9c349b50</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T22:57:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-zelensky-says-ukraine-ready-to-de-escalate-if-russia-halts-strikes--a60f2331197d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-zelensky-says-ukraine-ready-to-de-escalate-if-russia-halts-strikes" /><summary type="html">Ukraine is ready to halt attacks on Russian energy infrastructure if Moscow does the same, President Volodymyr Zelensky said Monday, after US President Donald Trump announced an apparent agreement between the two sides. Kyiv also warned that intensifying Russian strikes on Ukraine’s rail network are worsening each week.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'The very existence of LGBTQI people is seen as obscene', Turkish activist says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f17fb9ddd7df5ee6531876e7fa7264d969aa0c2d11ebad2e1c24f8ed51401176</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T21:02:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260914-the-very-existence-of-lgbtqi-people-is-seen-as-obscene-turkish-activist-says--f919faca8d4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260914-the-very-existence-of-lgbtqi-people-is-seen-as-obscene-turkish-activist-says" /><summary type="html">Turkish police on Sunday swooped into gay bars and the homes of LGBTQ activists, arresting at least 60 people in raids authorities said were aimed at boosting traditional family values, officials and activists said. Turkey's LGBTQ community has frequently been targeted by the government, with President Recep Tayyip Erdogan labelling it as a "deviant movement" of "perverts" responsible for the falling birth rate. In this edition, FRANCE 24's Monte Francis speaks with Yildiz Tar, Editor-in-Chief of KaosGL.org.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Dozens arrested in major anti-LGBTQ raids in Turkey</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8840426033ac6591f6eb4be8c70fde3defb62a524294cb7d4b6e0b0670bbf599</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T20:57:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/dozens-arrested-in-major-anti-lgbtq-raids-in-turkey--9f79aca6346a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/dozens-arrested-in-major-anti-lgbtq-raids-in-turkey" /><summary type="html">Turkish police on Sunday swooped into gay bars and the homes of LGBTQ activists, arresting at least 60 people in raids authorities said were aimed at boosting traditional family values, officials and activists said. Turkey's LGBTQ community has frequently been targeted by the government, with President Recep Tayyip Erdogan labelling it as a "deviant movement" of "perverts" responsible for the falling birth rate. In this edition, FRANCE 24's Monte Francis speaks with Yildiz Tar, Editor-in-Chief of KaosGL.org.</summary></entry><entry><title>Leaders urge EU to boost Arctic role to tackle Russia 'threat'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba26dd048363b8479899fe290cc5abd872e84f8b74d1ae5e5c5a6d2d5decc41a</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:06:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/leaders-urge-eu-to-boost-arctic-role-to-tackle-russia-threat--6fd38313421a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/leaders-urge-eu-to-boost-arctic-role-to-tackle-russia-threat" /><summary type="html">Twelve European countries meeting in Finland on Monday urged the European Union to beef up its presence in the Arctic, a geopolitical battleground caught between Russia and US President Donald Trump. FRANCE 24's Eliza Herbert reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Leaders urge EU to expand Arctic presence amid Russia 'threat'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5afc1642ecfffccaaa4e920f5622c47ac3fbcaf905e84d70793cd472c3b93fdf</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T17:41:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-leaders-urge-eu-to-expand-arctic-presence-amid-russia-threat--a416f27af86f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-leaders-urge-eu-to-expand-arctic-presence-amid-russia-threat" /><summary type="html">Twelve European countries on Monday called for the European Union to step up its presence in the Arctic, as melting ice opens new maritime routes while growing tensions with Russia and the United States increasingly put the region in the geopolitical spotlight.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Sweden faces political uncertainty after knife-edge election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3613730e95e00ca91af00575b5d0c455ecbe09e529bdf58261478d0228d63863</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T09:25:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-sweden-faces-political-uncertainty-after-knife-edge-election--2ea61f91582b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-sweden-faces-political-uncertainty-after-knife-edge-election" /><summary type="html">Sweden was bracing for a protracted struggle to form a government on Monday after election results showed a thin and uncertain lead for the left-wing opposition, while the far-right Sweden Democrats lost ground for the first time since entering parliament 16 years ago.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Sweden Election Aftermath: A hard night for the hard right?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b2f0415ae52a5258533acb3af55b8ff6b2a9fe8dc57d76ea14f13e44d39b801</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T19:04:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-sweden-election-aftermath-a-hard-night-for-the-hard-right--1acd06cf13c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-sweden-election-aftermath-a-hard-night-for-the-hard-right" /><summary type="html">FRANCE 24’s Gavin Lee speaks to Scandinavia Correspondent Trine Villeman for some analysis on how Sweden has voted in the 2026 election.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Sweden's centre-left holds razor-thin edge as exit polls show tight race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25db4af1300da725dff5a2ff32fd7cb5723fa18efde748b4d6ad875e89c14539</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T18:25:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-sweden-s-centre-left-opposition-leads-election-as-far-right-slips-exit-polls-show--96405fc870ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-sweden-s-centre-left-opposition-leads-election-as-far-right-slips-exit-polls-show" /><summary type="html">Sweden's general election remained too close to call early Monday, with nearly 90 percent of votes counted. Four opposition parties led by Social Democrat Magdalena Andersson held a one-seat parliamentary lead over Prime Minister Ulf Kristersson's right-wing bloc, which includes the Sweden Democrats, as both leaders said they were ready to govern.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine, Poland condemn Russia after drone strikes train near border</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f462b421ad317f8ed8370f1264007661d0e95f70d1067ec684ace95449526670</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T17:59:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-poland-ukraine-slam-russian-strikes-near-border-as-escalation--40ac44b5d486.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-poland-ukraine-slam-russian-strikes-near-border-as-escalation" /><summary type="html">Ukraine and Poland on Sunday condemned Russian strikes close to the Polish border as an "escalation" in the war, after drones struck a Warsaw-bound train. Ukraine's rail operator said former British PM Boris Johnson and ex-US CIA director David Petraeus were at a border train station nearby around the time the train was hit.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Sweden: Tight election puts all eyes on the far right</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92e3de1413ccdbb174280df0953675c11385eb1131e7e4f56b89d829f61f4ef4</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T15:55:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sweden-tight-election-puts-all-eyes-on-the-far-right--09fa155eb5fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/sweden-tight-election-puts-all-eyes-on-the-far-right" /><summary type="html">Swedes are voting in a closely fought general election that could see the far-right Sweden Democrats enter government for the first time. With immigration, crime and the economy dominating the campaign, Prime Minister Ulf Kristersson and Social Democrat leader Magdalena Andersson are locked in a neck-and-neck race.</summary></entry><entry><title>Swedish far-right eyes role in government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:316a41b34137d7dde0d62372894120244cd8f925004cac21dffa02e5f32c7008</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T13:11:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/swedish-far-right-eyes-role-in-government--71417d1eac6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/swedish-far-right-eyes-role-in-government" /><summary type="html">As Sweden heads into a closely fought election, the far right is gaining ground by tapping into concerns over crime and security, issues that some voters increasingly associate with migration. On FRANCE 24, Stockholm University sociologist Zeth Isaksson said the movement has also softened its image in recent years, making it more acceptable to a broader electorate, while also cautioning against overstating the strength of the far right in Sweden.</summary></entry><entry><title>Sweden election: A turning point for the far right?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d5800361730b344769004d4e18464943a412d344a19698b9ea75433fb2b4635</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:48:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sweden-election-a-turning-point-for-the-far-right--b7d3156e03ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/sweden-election-a-turning-point-for-the-far-right" /><summary type="html">The stakes are high in Sweden's general election, with the far right poised to enter government for the first time. TV4 News journalist Markus Karlsson-Bourrioux explains how opinion polls shifted from a comfortable centre-left lead to a tight race over the summer, and how far-right ideas have gained ground since the last election in 2022.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany: Thousands rally against far-right after AfD victory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46d50cd0ff3b5986844deedfd8b76197d3c418b2cec7be6c717a4bc67fe97399</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:41:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/germany-thousands-rally-against-far-right-after-afd-victory--32004fba5832.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/germany-thousands-rally-against-far-right-after-afd-victory" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of people marched in around 20 cities across Germany to protest the rise of the far right after the AfD's historic victory in the Saxony-Anhalt state election. Demonstrators said they were defending democracy as mainstream parties continue to rule out governing with the AfD.</summary></entry><entry><title>Swedes vote in close general election that could usher far right into government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d63dc1e67cb8566732ad0cf4c40c2fff847ff501c2d723f466dcd3ea57ff2717</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T06:16:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-swedes-vote-in-close-general-election-that-could-usher-far-right-into-government--d9796cd3be30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-swedes-vote-in-close-general-election-that-could-usher-far-right-into-government" /><summary type="html">Swedes are heading to the polls Sunday for a general election that will either bring a far right party into government for the first time or shift the country back towards the liberalism it has long been known for. The centre-left opposition holds a narrow lead over the ruling right-wing bloc but Prime ⁠Minister Ulf Kristersson's four-party alliance – which includes the far right Sweden Democrats – has been catching up in the final weeks of campaigning.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands protest against far-right AfD party in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4679fcf0b91d088ad2fd4059a65232cb0de84ca9554817ec68c64a47feeb329</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T17:12:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-tens-of-thousands-of-people-protest-in-germany-against-far-right-afd--de7794873779.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-tens-of-thousands-of-people-protest-in-germany-against-far-right-afd" /><summary type="html">About 150,000 demonstrators took to the streets in around 20 cities across Germany on Saturday against the far-right AfD, after the party scored a crushing victory in a state election last week. The Alternative for Germany (AfD) topped the vote in the eastern region of Saxony-Anhalt, and is now seeking to form the first extreme-right state government in Germany since World War II.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Kremlin says meeting between Putin and Zelensky at Miami G20 'impossible'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1856e206fbcf10ebe1fb82aa21abc46da42d4ba30712a8642781773d307caccf</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T09:27:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-zelensky-willing-to-meet-putin-at-g20-kremlin-still-to-confirm-attendance--05231991019c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-zelensky-willing-to-meet-putin-at-g20-kremlin-still-to-confirm-attendance" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said he was willing to meet Russian leader Vladimir Putin at the G20 summit in Miami for talks on ending the war. However, the Kremlin immediately ruled it out, saying it was "impossible" and that a meeting would only take place in Russian capital Moscow.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French police suspect Normandy train derailment was result of sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:969ba2d71909c1e687c3e9abf8d573a6493783b1892107ca6645f4813f9517f0</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T08:48:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-french-police-investigate-suspected-sabotage-in-train-derailment--cc176be772bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-french-police-investigate-suspected-sabotage-in-train-derailment" /><summary type="html">A police source said Saturday that French investigators suspect sabotage caused a train derailment in northwest France after a fragment of rail was found on the track. At least 44 people were injured in the derailment that occurred a day earlier, including an 18-year-old woman "in a critical condition".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says unified Ireland ‘would be fantastic' during Dublin trip</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd97d7c8f9fd778b257305ff87b350f04a2c6f25d172eabd55fbe401ad4ca08f</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T07:51:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-trump-arrives-in-dublin-for-talks-with-ireland-s-leaders-before-attending-golf-tournament--dec783fc4bf2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-trump-arrives-in-dublin-for-talks-with-ireland-s-leaders-before-attending-golf-tournament" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Saturday said a unified Ireland would be “fantastic" during a weekend visit to a major tournament at his Irish golf course. The two-day trip to Ireland is the latest example of how the US leader blends his official duties with his personal interests.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
